+
+## Room & Materials
+
+- Welcome/check-in zone: Place an entrance table with an alphabetized set of 28 name badges, a sign-in sheet, blank accessibility note cards, pens, and the day’s one-page schedule.
+- Plenary zone: Arrange 28 participant chairs so both pilot teams can see the facilitator and shared display; provide a facilitator station, flip-chart pads, markers, sticky notes, and a visible timer.
+- Breakout zones: Mark two clearly labeled breakout areas with a flip-chart pad, markers, sticky notes, dependency-map sheets, action cards, and a timer in each area; leave a clear route between both areas and the plenary seats.
+
+## Communications
+
+Subject: Northstar Pilot Forum — October 22 details
+
+Hello Northstar participants,
+
+We’re looking forward to bringing the two pilot teams together for the Northstar Pilot Forum on Thursday, October 22, 2026, from 09:00–16:00 CT in Cedar Studio.
